@startuml
title Conexión y persistencia de datos
hide footbox
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontColor #123B52
skinparam ArrowColor #1E5A78
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #E9F3F7
skinparam participantBorderColor #1E5A78
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

actor "Browser" as Browser
participant "Next.js\n127.0.0.1:3000" as Next
participant "Route Handlers\n/api/session/*, /api/patient/*" as Proxy
participant "Spring Boot REST\nhost :18080 / contenedor :8080" as Spring
participant "Service" as Service
participant "Spring Data JPA\nHibernate ORM" as ORM
participant "JDBC\nDriver PostgreSQL" as JDBC
database "PostgreSQL 16 Docker\nhost :55432 / postgres:5432\nhospital_platform" as PG

== Solicitud del paciente ==
Browser -> Next : HTTP
Next -> Proxy : fetch mismo origen
Proxy -> Spring : BACKEND_URL / JWT
Spring -> Service : reglas de negocio
Service -> ORM : Repository
ORM -> JDBC : SQL
JDBC -> PG : SQL por red Docker
PG --> JDBC : filas
JDBC --> ORM : resultados
ORM --> Service : resultado
Service --> Spring : DTO
Spring --> Proxy : JSON + estado
Proxy --> Browser : respuesta

== Arranque del backend ==
participant "Flyway" as Flyway
collections "Migraciones\nV1 · V2 · V3 · V4 · V5" as Migrations
Flyway -> Migrations : V1 → V2 → V3 → V4 → V5
Migrations -> PG : aplica cada migración en orden

note over Service, JDBC
  La reserva usa CapacityGateway y JdbcTemplate
  directamente sobre JDBC.
end note
note over Spring, PG
  La contraseña y el secreto JWT se leen del entorno;
  no se incluyen en el diagrama.
end note
@enduml
